---
/**
 * Wave-3 spoke page body — Mayan vs. Chinese Gender Dual Calculator.
 * Side-by-side ancient folklore comparisons, dual interactive predictor,
 * mathematical parity vs. lunisolar matrix breakdown, and clinical genetics demarcation.
 */
import MayanDualPredictor from '@components/calculators/MayanDualPredictor.tsx';
import FaqAccordion from '@theme/components/FaqAccordion.astro';
import RelatedTools from '@theme/components/RelatedTools.astro';
import GeoLeadLinks from '@theme/components/GeoLeadLinks.astro';
import { MAYAN_DUAL_STRINGS, MAYAN_DUAL_FAQ } from '@i18n/tools';
import { toolStrings } from '@i18n/tools.locales';
import { getDictionary } from '@i18n/translations';
import type { Locale } from '@i18n/utils';

interface Props { locale?: Locale; }
const { locale = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const t = getDictionary(locale);
const S = toolStrings(MAYAN_DUAL_STRINGS, locale, 'mayanDual');
---

<div class="pt-10">
  <div class="section-shell grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr]">
    <div>
      <p class="chip mb-4">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-red-500 to-amber-500"></span>
        Ancient civilizational showdown · China vs. Maya
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-[2.35rem] font-extrabold leading-[1.1] text-plum-900 sm:text-5xl">
        Mayan vs. Chinese Gender Predictor: <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-red-600 via-girl-500 to-amber-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">Dual Ancient Calculator</span>
      </h1>
      <span class="mt-4 block h-1.5 w-16 rounded-full" aria-hidden="true" style="background-image: linear-gradient(to right, #dc2626, #d97706); box-shadow: 0 4px 10px -3px rgba(220,38,38,.45);"></span>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-plum-600" set:html={S.lead} />

      {/* SEO / GEO link equity funnel within first 100 words */}
      <GeoLeadLinks />

      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-red-500"></span>Qing Palace 28×12 Matrix</span>
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>Mayan Parity Math</span>
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-purple-500"></span>Synergy vs. Split Detection</span>
      </div>

      {/* Clinical & Scientific Demarcation Card */}
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-3xl p-5" style="border: 1px solid transparent; background: linear-gradient(rgba(253,242,248,.65), rgba(253,242,248,.65)) padding-box, linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(238,90,151,.3), rgba(217,119,6,.3)) border-box;">
        <p class="font-display font-bold text-plum-800">🔬 Medical &amp; Clinical Demarcation Notice</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-plum-600">
          Biological sex is determined strictly at the moment of fertilization by whether the sperm cell delivers an
          <strong>X chromosome</strong> (female, XX) or a <strong>Y chromosome</strong> (male, XY). A comprehensive
          peer-reviewed epidemiological study of <strong>2.8 million Swedish births</strong> published by Villamor et al. (2010)
          demonstrated conclusively that ancient calendar prediction methods match a random <strong>50% coin flip</strong>.
          Neither chart possesses clinical predictive accuracy. For verified prenatal sex assessment, consult your OB/GYN regarding
          <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/understanding/testing/nipt/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="font-semibold underline decoration-girl-400 hover:text-plum-900">MedlinePlus NIPT screening</a>
          or the <a href="https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/routine-tests-during-pregnancy" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="font-semibold underline decoration-girl-400 hover:text-plum-900">ACOG guidelines for mid-pregnancy ultrasound</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 min-h-[520px]">
      <MayanDualPredictor client:idle strings={S} />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section-shell mt-14">
    <div class="prose-custom max-w-4xl">
      <h2>How the Mayan Parity Engine Works vs. the Chinese Lunisolar Matrix</h2>
      <p>
        While modern folklore frequently groups ancient baby predictors together, the <strong>Ancient Mayan</strong> and
        <strong>Imperial Chinese</strong> methods originated thousands of miles apart and operated on entirely different
        cosmological, mathematical, and calendrical systems:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The Mayan Parity System:</strong> The Maya civilization of Mesoamerica was renowned for advanced mathematical
          vigesimal (base-20) arithmetic and the sacred 260-day <em>Tzolk’in</em> calendar. The popular gender folklore derived from
          their traditions uses a modular parity calculation: take the mother's solar age at conception and the Gregorian conception
          month. If both numbers share the same parity (both even or both odd), folklore predicts a <strong>Girl</strong>. If one is even
          and the other is odd (mixed parity), folklore predicts a <strong>Boy</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The Chinese Lunisolar System:</strong> Originating from the Qing Dynasty imperial court, the Chinese gender chart
          relies on an astronomical lunisolar calendar. It measures the mother's <em>Xūsuì</em> (virtual lunar age, where conception
          in the womb counts as year one, incrementing each Chinese New Year) against the astronomical lunar month of conception,
          reading a fixed 28-row by 12-column matrix preserved in Beijing archives.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why Ancient Cultures Disagree on ~50% of Dates (Folklore Split)</h2>
      <p>
        Because the Mayan calculation uses Western solar calendar years and Gregorian months, while the Chinese chart uses
        astronomical lunisolar months and Chinese New Year cutoffs, the two systems track entirely divergent time cycles.
        Around 50% of all conception dates yield a <strong>Folklore Split</strong> (one system predicts Boy while the other predicts Girl).
        Neither system is "broken" when they disagree—they simply measure unrelated arithmetic patterns.
      </p>

      <h2>Ancient Civilizational Comparison: China vs. Maya</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-3xl bg-white/70 shadow-soft ring-1 ring-cream-200">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[680px] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <caption class="sr-only">Detailed comparison of Chinese vs Mayan baby gender predictors</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-plum-800 text-white">
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-display text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm">Feature</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-display text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm">🇨🇳 Ancient Chinese Predictor</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-display text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm">🏺 Ancient Mayan Predictor</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-plum-700">
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200 bg-red-50/30">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Historical Origin</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Qing Dynasty royal tomb / imperial palace (c. 1644–1912 CE)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Pre-Columbian Mesoamerican civilization (c. 2000 BCE–1500 CE)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Calendar Baseline</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Chinese lunisolar calendar (astronomical new moons + leap months)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Gregorian/solar months with Tzolk’in-inspired parity arithmetic</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200 bg-amber-50/30">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Mother's Age Formula</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Traditional Lunar Age (<em>Xūsuì</em>: birth year to conception year + 1)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Western chronological age at conception (completed solar years)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Mathematical Logic</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Empirical 28×12 lookup matrix (ages 18–45 × months 1–12)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Binary parity: even/even or odd/odd = Girl; mixed = Boy</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200 bg-red-50/30">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Scientific Accuracy</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">~50% (equivalent to a coin toss, Swedish study 2010)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">~50% (mathematical parity has no biological mechanism)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Gold-Standard Clinical Test</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3" colspan="2">
                NIPT (cell-free fetal DNA blood test, 99%+ accuracy from 10 weeks) or 18–20 week anatomy ultrasound
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Double Folklore Synergy: What Happens When Both Agree?</h2>
      <p>
        When both the Chinese and Mayan engines calculate the same sex, parents often ask whether the dual prediction
        increases real-world probability. Mathematically and biologically, it does not: because neither folklore method has
        any causal link to chromosomal fertilization, two independent 50% random variables still yield a 50% likelihood.
        However, in the world of baby shower games, nursery theme planning, and lighthearted anticipation, a
        <strong>Double Synergy verdict</strong> serves as a beloved historical curiosity!
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell mt-14" aria-labelledby="mayan-dual-faq">
    <h2 id="mayan-dual-faq" class="section-title text-center">Frequently Asked Questions: Mayan vs. Chinese Gender Prediction</h2>
    <div class="mt-6"><FaqAccordion items={MAYAN_DUAL_FAQ} /></div>
  </section>

  <RelatedTools t={t} locale={locale} exclude="mayan-gender-predictor-calculator/" />
</div>
